<title>USA: Northwest provides Red River relief freigh.</title>
<headline>Northwest provides Red River relief freigh.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northwest Airlines said it is providing a Boeing 747-200 freighter for a special airlift Sunday of over 200,000 pounds of relief supplies for victims of the Red River floods which have affected thousands in the states of North Dakota and Minnesota.</p>
<p>The 747 freighter, handled and flown by Northwest volunteers, will fly the donated supplies to Grand Forks Air Base in North Dakota.</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542-7706 Fax+5017</p>
